<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Hashemite Kingdom of Jordan</h1><p class="st-meta">1946 CE – present · capital Amman</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The kingdom of the Hashemite dynasty east of the Jordan, which has survived regional wars and hosts millions of refugees.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> recognised the independence of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/emirate-of-transjordan">Emirate of Transjordan</a> in 1946, and on 25 May the emir <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdullah-i-of-jordan">Abdullah I</a> became king; the country was renamed Jordan in 1949. In the 1948 war the Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">Legion</a> held the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-bank">West Bank</a> and East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>, which Jordan annexed in 1950.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Jordan is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitutional-monarchy">constitutional monarchy</a> in which the king holds wide powers. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdullah-i-of-jordan">Abdullah I</a> was assassinated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> in 1951; after the brief reign of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/talal-of-jordan">Talal</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hussein-of-jordan">Hussein</a> ruled from 1953 to 1999. Jordan lost the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-bank">West Bank</a> to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-israel">Israel</a> in 1967 and expelled the Palestinian armed groups in the conflict of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-september">Black September</a> in 1970. It has relied on foreign aid, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phosphate">phosphates</a> and remittances, and its population is largely of Palestinian origin.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hussein-of-jordan">Hussein</a> signed a peace treaty with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-israel">Israel</a> in 1994. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdullah-ii-of-jordan">Abdullah II</a> succeeded him in 1999 and has kept the monarchy stable while hosting large numbers of Iraqi and Syrian refugees.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/hashemite-kingdom-of-jordan.jpg" alt="Hashemite Kingdom of Jordan" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Jordan.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1946 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Amman</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abdullah I, Hussein, Abdullah II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/jordan">Jordan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Jordan, Kingdom of Jordan</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1986&amp;focus=hashemite-kingdom-of-jordan" aria-label="Hashemite Kingdom of Jordan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5605 1015 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Hashemite Kingdom of Jordan lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5925 1271L5925 1271"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5925 1271h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5925 1271h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5925 1271h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Amman. <a href="/atlas?year=1986&amp;focus=hashemite-kingdom-of-jordan">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
